# Production host crontab. `sudo crontab -e`.
#
# The probe runs every minute. That is not for detection speed — every threshold
# in it is measured in minutes — but because the "more than three in five
# minutes" conditions are evaluated from a series of samples, and a five-minute
# cadence would give them one sample per window.

*/1 * * * * /opt/qoida/qoida-platform/infra/observability/qoida-probe.sh >/dev/null 2>&1

# The backup, which touches the stamp file the probe reads. See
# docs/runbooks/restore.md.
30 3 * * * /opt/qoida/qoida-platform/infra/production/run-backup.sh >/dev/null 2>&1

# REMOVE THIS LINE when the probe above is installed. heartbeat.sh evaluates five
# checks at one tier and withholds the dead-man's-switch ping for any of them,
# which turns a disk at 86% into a night alert and breaks ADR 0034's budget of
# three. qoida-probe.sh supersedes it.
#
# */5 * * * * /opt/qoida/qoida-platform/infra/production/heartbeat.sh
